NOTICE — aa-intelligence-index-reverse
======================================

Last updated: 2026-09-02

1. What this project is
-----------------------
An independent, community reconstruction of the scoring formula behind the
**Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index** (methodology v4.1.1), shipped as:

- a machine-readable weights table (`data/weights_v4.1.1.csv`)
- a machine-readable matrix of public component scores (`data/models.csv`)
- a small, dependency-free calculator (`src/aa_index.py`)
- a worked example reproducing the published Index of 8 models to within
  |Delta| <= 0.31 (see `examples/` and the README)

2. Non-affiliation
------------------
This project is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to
Artificial Analysis, or to any model provider whose models appear in the
data files (Anthropic, xAI, Moonshot AI, Z.ai, Alibaba, Google, etc.).
"Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index", "GDPval-AA", "AA-LCR" and all
related benchmark names are the property of their respective owners.

3. Data provenance
------------------
- The weights come from the public methodology pages of Artificial
  Analysis (v4.1.1):
  https://artificialanalysis.ai/methodology/intelligence-benchmarking
  https://artificialanalysis.ai/evaluations/artificial-analysis-intelligence-index
  https://artificialanalysis.ai/articles/artificial-analysis-intelligence-index-v4-1
- The component scores (the "s_i" values in `data/models.csv`) were read
  from publicly displayed charts/dumps on artificialanalysis.ai on
  2026-09-01/02. No private data, no scraped paywalled content, no
  redistribution of raw HTML.
- The "Index AA" column in `data/models.csv` is the value publicly
  displayed by Artificial Analysis for each model at the same date.

4. What you may do
------------------
- Reuse the formula, the code and the data files with attribution
  (MIT for code; the weights themselves are CC BY 4.0 via Artificial
  Analysis — attribute Artificial Analysis when redistributing them).
- Submit PRs to add models: each new row MUST include the source URL and
  the date of the AA chart dump (see CONTRIBUTING.md).

5. Known limits (do not oversell the result)
--------------------------------------------
- The reconstruction was validated ONLY on the v4.1.1 Index band ~56-63
  (8 models, max |Delta| 0.30). The v4.3.2 weights + calculator have NO
  completed public-dump validation yet — that is the top roadmap item.
- All deltas are <= 0, consistent with rounding noise in the public
  component scores, not with a structural formula error.
- The Elo <-> model-variant mapping (e.g. "Grok 4.6 (high)") was done by
  hand; a wrong row would fail loudly in recomputation, the other rows
  would not be affected.
